        "priority": "P1",
        "title": "Let natural-grace expiry escape process discovery",
        "path": "docs/versioning/2026-10-08-resource-combined-validation/runner.py",
        "line": 318,
        "createdAtUtc": "2026-10-08T01:32:55Z",
        "resolved": false,
        "outdated": false,
        "originalText": "When a child is first discovered near the end of the 60-second natural-close window, any `NaturalGraceExpired` raised by `register()` is caught by `discover()`'s broad `except Exception` and converted into a pending-identity error before this handler can see it. That error is added to `monitor_errors`, so the run remains `FAILED` even if the subsequent TERM window closes every process successfully—the same normal-boundary condition this V04 delta is intended to correct. Re-raise `NaturalGraceExpired` from `discover()` before handling ordinary identity failures."
      }
    ],
